  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Municipal Support for Disaster Risk Reduction in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) is at an increasing risk of disasters due to climate change and environmental degradation, while facing systemic political and socio-economic issues preventing comprehensive preparedness and risk reduction.Climate change projections for BiH predict increases in natural disasters&apos; frequency, unpredictability and intensity, which could exacerbate existing political and social tensions. The floods of 2014 can serve as a warning sign for future events. In 2014 the country experienced devastating floods that affected one in four inhabitants and resulted in significant economic losses. BiH is also at risk of other disasters, most prominently landslides, heat waves, forest fires, and earthquakes. &#x200B;This project will support the authorities in the  people-centered approach to improving the safety, security, and well-being of people in hazard-prone areas, with a focus on improving key infrastructure to reduce risks of disasters.  This project is complimentary to the community infrastructure component that is itself part of larger EU-funded Migration Response program. The community infrastructure component provides communities along the migration route with infrastructure projects. Recently several communities along the migration route were hit by severe floods, highlighting the need for DRR infrastructure projects to protect the communities from future floods. The assessments and planning was finalized by IOM engineers. The municipal authorities requested to contribute to the project. This project will thus be used to operationalize the funding from the Municipalities and is closely linked to the EU contribution.</narrative>
  </description>
